Subject: gpu-libs archive the identity bridge whole on Linux
Why: AC-T7.4.1: meson makes a static library it does not install (the identity bridge's, install: false) a thin archive on Linux (GNU ar's T), whose member names an object in gpu-libs' scratch, which it removes as it ends; cargo then fails bundling it into the GPU VM process (shards-vmm: failed to open object file). Reproduced on 00aad (Linux x86_64, meson 1.11.2): OUT/libshards_gpu_selection.a was 272 bytes of '!<thin>'. Archived whole from its object with ar rcsD, as gpu-libs archives the render server's; macOS and Windows unchanged.

diff --git a/scripts/gpu-libs b/scripts/gpu-libs
index d5eecc9f7feb3f33bdfe67667de67746bc0967ae..9b7235bbd2e4c4db929e6e8e18c6f88bd442f6e3 100755
--- a/scripts/gpu-libs
+++ b/scripts/gpu-libs
@@ -290,6 +290,12 @@ ninja --quiet -C "$(native "$work/selection")"
 if [[ $host == Windows-* ]]; then
     cp "$work/selection/shards_gpu_selection.lib" "$out/"
     libs+=(shards_gpu_selection.lib)
+elif [[ $host == Linux-* ]]; then
+    # meson makes a library it does not install a thin archive (GNU ar's T), whose members name
+    # objects in this build's scratch, removed as it ends: the bridge's object archived whole,
+    # as the render server's are.
+    ar rcsD "$out/libshards_gpu_selection.a" "$work/selection/libshards_gpu_selection.a.p/"*.o
+    libs+=(libshards_gpu_selection.a)
 else
     cp "$work/selection/libshards_gpu_selection.a" "$out/"
     libs+=(libshards_gpu_selection.a)
